{"reference":"Jeremiah 34","book":"Jeremiah","chapter":34,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"In the Book of Jeremiah","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Jeremiah belongs to a book that brings together several forms of material, including poetry, prose sermons, narratives, letters, headings, restoration collections, oracles concerning nations, and an appendix. Its long compositional and textual history is disputed. A practical outline places chapters 34–45 together, without settling how the book was composed.","confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed","provenance_refs":["reader_path_jeremiah_034_97456dbc3d576cc318284368"]}]}],"generated_metadata":null}